  "delta": {
    "modern_url_elicitation": "CHANGED: modern requests declare elicitation form and url capabilities. A live URL input_required round retries tools/call with action cancel in headless mode and echoes requestState. Interactive acceptance and browser completion were not tested.",
    "legacy_elicitation": "UNCHANGED: explicit legacy and v1 initialize declare bare elicitation. Auto fallback first discovers with form and url, then initializes with bare elicitation.",
    "tasks": "UNCHANGED: no legacy tasks or tasks extension declared in any case. The task gate remains literally false; bundled task methods are legacy, with no tasks/update or bare notifications/tasks.",
    "direct_http_default": "UNCHANGED: isolated default and v2-only negotiate 2026-07-28 with discover and catalog listen.",
    "listen": "UNCHANGED: notification refetch, dropped-stream reopen/reconciliation, and unmatched-ack cancellation remain functional.",
    "resource_visibility": "CHANGED: official notes and bundled consumer filter exclude MCP Apps UI resources from model resource lists; URI reads remain available. Static evidence only."
  },
  "methodology": {
    "static": "Exact-byte counts and bounded inspection of readable embedded JavaScript. Literal vocabulary presence is not proof of reachable behavior. Counts increased with bundle layout changes and are not feature counts.",
    "live": "Unmodified installed binary, --bare -p, --tools '' (empty built-in tool set), --setting-sources '', --strict-mcp-config, explicit loopback-only MCP fixture, --debug-file. Each case used a fresh temporary cwd and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR under env -i with HOME preserved; CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, --bare, empty setting sources and strict MCP config provide fixture isolation. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY was a dummy value and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL pointed to a local deterministic Messages stub holding its first response for 8 s so list-change delivery was observable. No real model inference or shared-service mutation. Fixtures: fixtures/claude-mcp-fixture.py, fixtures/claude-messages-stub.py, fixtures/claude-audit-matrix.sh. The URL case allows only mcp__fixture__fixture_echo and uses STUB_TOOL_CALL=1 to produce one deterministic tool call before the final text response.",
    "fixture": "Discover advertised 2026-07-28 and 2025-11-25, all three catalog listChanged capabilities, resources.subscribe and the io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks extension. Listen answered as chunked SSE with the acknowledgement first, its subscription id equal to the listen request id, then tools/resources/prompts list_changed after waiting up to 10 s for the first tools/list and another 1 s. Healthy cases list before emission; in the unmatched-ack case the bounded wait expires, so the first notifications precede catalog startup at about 25 s. The legacy fixture rejected discover with -32601 and answered initialize at the requested version with Mcp-Session-Id and legacy tasks advertised, holding the GET stream. The drop fixture closed the first listen stream right after the notifications with no terminal JSON-RPC result. The unmatched-ack case substitutes a server-minted subscription id. Four added cases cover default fallback, each explicit legacy opt-out, and mismatched acknowledgement. A tenth case returns a modern URL elicitation without elicitationId, then completes with an error result describing cancellation after the client retries with inputResponses.",
    "limits": [
      "Account-specific remote rollout flags were not inspected; isolated defaults are not a universal rollout verdict.",
      "Prompt/resource catalogs were empty; only tool refetches were observed after list_changed notifications.",
      "No task result was returned to a client that did not declare support. Task execution and task notifications were not tested.",
      "No per-URI resource subscription, interactive URL acceptance, browser completion, form elicitation, or prolonged reconnect/parking behavior was live-tested.",
      "Cache hint expiry and cache sharing were not live-tested. Catalog notifications caused tool refetches despite a 60000 ms fixture TTL.",
      "The claude.ai connector projection headers and MCP Apps resource filtering were inspected statically only."
    ],
    "raw_evidence_directory": "/tmp/claude-2.1.281-mcp-audit-20260923-final",
    "static_evidence_file": "/tmp/claude-2.1.281-static-20260923.txt",
    "capture_validation": "All ten cases passed a fresh complete matrix with HOME preserved and EXPECT_TASKS=absent, then passed AUDIT_VERIFY_ONLY=1 replay. The URL verifier requires form/url capabilities, exactly one MRTR retry, action cancel, unchanged tool name/arguments, exact requestState echo, delivery of the cancellation result to the model, and no URL visit. Negative replays removing inputResponses, changing requestState or removing final tool results each exited 1. Python fixture compilation, bash -n and git diff --check passed."
  },
